diff --git a/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md b/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
index 4c98f6b..ff8904d 100644
--- a/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
+++ b/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
@@ -16,9 +16,120 @@ logos belong to their owners.
 - Display name DeepSeek Harness rewritten to Crew Harness in prose docs only.
 - This file and a README banner added.
 
-## Not done yet (stage 2)
+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
 
-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
+Upstream is a developer preview (root package.json version 0.2.1-alpha.1 at the
+pinned commit; the catalog row still quotes the older README figure
+0.1.0-rc.5). Every claim below is a claim about that preview.
+
+- Model plugin -> OpenVault `/v1`. The base bundle and the sdk-minimal bundle
+  mount one OpenAI-compatible route, `openvault`, on `dsh-llm-pi-ai` at
+  `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1`), model
+  `auto` (OpenVault's catalog pick). New Agents and the ACP server default to
+  provider `openvault`. The direct DeepSeek rows (`llm-deepseek`,
+  `llm-deepseek-account`) are not mounted. The only credential reference in
+  the default config is `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY`, the caller's issued `ov_`
+  identity; no provider key field (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and the like) remains.
+  The keyed DeepSeek search route is gone; `web_search` stays in the tool
+  catalog and fails loud at call time (`WEB_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE`) until a
+  search route through OpenVault exists.
+- Tool and sandbox plugins register only under the Crew gate. New package
+  `packages/guard/crew-gate` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-crew-gate`) ports the Netie
+  contract shape: `POST ${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/api/crew/gate` with
+  `{kind, id, intent, parent_run_id, child_id}` and nothing else; a body key
+  (`skill_body`, `prompt`, `instructions`, `transcript`), an unregistered
+  kind, a missing URL, a transport failure or a reply without `allowed: true`
+  is a refusal. It mounts a `tools/pre-execute` listener, so every tool body
+  waits for `allowed: true`. The tool registry (`tools.crewGate: required`)
+  and the sandbox provider (`sandbox-local crewGate: required`) inject the
+  gate and refuse registration with a visible error while it is absent.
+- Names: the `dsh` help line, the `dsh web` help line, the Web GUI prompt and
+  URL description, the onboarding brand and the plugin-manager safety line
+  say Crew Harness. The official client build title says Crew Harness.
+- Upstream tests that pinned the old brand now state the new value (none
+  deleted or skipped): `apps/cli/tests/plugin.spec.ts` inline snapshot, four
+  onboarding snapshot files, the acp-app and sdk-minimal specs, the client
+  build title spec. The Cordis catalog generator maps `crewGate` to
+  `docs/subsystems/sandbox.md` and exempts the `GateAsk` type; generated docs
+  were regenerated, not edited.
+- Gate tests, in the upstream runner: `packages/bundle/base/tests/netie-defaults.spec.ts`
+  (the shipped patch files parsed and evaluated by the real loader) and
+  `packages/guard/crew-gate/tests/crew-gate.spec.ts` (the live registry).
+  Both fail on the upstream defaults.
+
+## Changed in stage 3 work (launch readiness; stage number stays 2, see below)
+
+- SDK code defaults follow the composition: the TypeScript SDK client, the
+  Python SDK and the `subagent-dsh-sdk` child runtime default to provider
+  `openvault`, model `auto`. The SDK JSON-RPC server no longer mounts the
+  DeepSeek adapter on demand when a caller names `deepseek-official`: a
+  provider without a mounted adapter is refused, whichever it is.
+- Upstream e2e and snapshot fixtures that patched the removed `llm-deepseek`
+  rows by id now insert the adapter they exercise; the two DeepSeek adapter
+  packages stay resolvable from the base bundle so those scenarios still run,
+  but no shipped profile mounts them. The recorded-session corpora
+  (`snapshots/session`, `snapshots/acp`, `snapshots/sdk`) replay with no
+  OpenVault, so their test compositions switch the Crew gate off the same way
+  they already switch the permission mode to `danger-full-access` under
+  `DSH_SNAPSHOT`: `crew-gate` disabled, `tools` and `sandbox` `crewGate: off`.
+  The CLI expected-output fixtures under `apps/cli/tests` carry the same
+  override. Test composition only; no shipped profile carries it.
+- Gate ask ids: the parent is the agent's session id; a nested dispatch inside
+  an already gated call names its root call id; a root call with no agent is
+  refused.
+- Product copy: the Models welcome notice and the Office preview notice say
+  Crew Harness. Copy that names the DeepSeek account sign-in (Settings,
+  Account; onboarding credit text) still says DeepSeek, because that is the
+  vendor account it signs into, not this product.
+- Launch readiness proof, in the upstream's expected-output runner:
+  `apps/cli/tests/profiles/headless/tests/netie-launch.expected.e2e.ts` boots
+  the shipped headless profile from source against a stand-in that serves
+  `/v1/chat/completions` and `/api/crew/gate`. It asserts the model request
+  goes to `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1` with `Authorization: Bearer
+  $NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY` and model `auto`, that the tool body runs only after
+  the gate answered `allowed: true` to an ids-only ask, and that a refusal
+  reaches the session log as the tool's `CREW_GATE_DENIED` error with the
+  tool never run. The stand-in is not OpenVault: it proves the wire shape and
+  the wiring, not OpenVault's decisions.
+
+## What an operator needs for Crew Harness to run (launch readiness)
+
+Measured here: `pnpm run build` passes (CLI, SDK runtime, web client), the
+built `dsh --help` and `dsh --profile headless --dump-config` show the Crew
+Harness name, the `openvault` route, the `crew-gate` row and the gated
+registry, and the headless profile completes a turn with a tool call against
+the stand-in above.
+
+Required at launch, by the shipped defaults:
+
+1. OpenVault reachable at `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000`)
+   serving an OpenAI-compatible `POST /v1/chat/completions` with streaming.
+   TAS-OPENVAULT measures `/v1` as FreeRoute (assumed to accept model `auto`
+   as its catalog pick; whether it refuses a call without the `ov_` key in
+   `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY` is not measured).
+2. OpenVault serving `POST /api/crew/gate` and answering `allowed: true` for
+   `kind: service` asks. Per TAS-OPENVAULT section 8 this endpoint is a patch
+   (`docs/patches/openvault-crew-gate.patch`, OpenVault PR #44), not OpenVault
+   main. Until it lands, every tool call in this product is refused, visibly.
+   That is the one blocker between this fork and a stage 3 claim.
+3. `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY` set in the launching environment (a credential
+   reference, never written to a config file).
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+
+- Package scope `@deepseek-ai/*`, the `dsh` binary name, the `DSH_*` env
+  names, the `~/.dsh` home, the Desktop app and container names: each needs
+  a build and a rebase plan to rename. About 190 further "DeepSeek Harness"
+  strings sit in package.json descriptions, zh locale strings and prompts.
+- The DeepSeek account sign-in platform row (`deepseek-account`) and the Web
+  Models page onboarding dialog still exist; they are not a model route.
+- Sandbox confinement calls are not posted individually; the tool call that
+  spawns them is.
+- The ACP model picker lists provider groups in adapter activation order,
+  which is not deterministic once two routes are mounted; the ACP snapshot
+  corpus therefore mounts only its recorded route. A `skill` kind is refused until OpenVault has a registry row.
+- Whether OpenVault `/v1` refuses a call without `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY`, and
+  whether it serves `/v1/models`, is not measured here.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
 - Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Model plugin -> OpenVault /v1. Tool and sandbox plugins register only through Cortex tool_runner.
